  "description": "Story CC-7.10 D5: the screen budget both platforms enforce. limits start at the epic AC values. known is the ratchet: each entry is a violation the current app has, owned by the Epic 7 story that removes it; the guard fails on a new, larger, smaller or vanished one. paragraph-lines entries list each paragraph as {key, lines}, its measured line count. scripts/check-screen-budget-decisions.mjs compares this file with its merge base: a raised limit (it then needs a limitDecisions entry), an added known entry, a raised known value, a new element key or a paragraph with more lines must cite a decision the base never used, and every cited decision must be recorded in the decidedIn story's spec under '## Screen budget decisions' as one or more term lines: '- <decision>: `rule=<rule> scope=<platform>/<screen>/<fixture> max=<value>`' for known entries (any segment may be *; paragraph-lines adds lines=<most lines per paragraph>), or '- <decision>: `rule=<rule> scope=limit max=<value>`' for a limit. The JSON value must be within a term's rule, scope and max.",
